title: Budget and the Costs of the Crisis
subtitle: Answer the cabinet's package before the Sejm votes on it.
is-pinned-card: true
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishProjects.budgetCardAvailable(Q) !}
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
// Card parliament.finance_amendment (technical reference 17.10; card catalogue 7.3): open while a package
// of this cabinet waits for its vote and PPS is in the cabinet or supports it (decision 5 of stage 4).
// One answer for 0 T; the partners judge a PPS condition by 8.3.
var view = PolishProjects.budgetView(Q);
Q.pl_bud_package = view.package;
Q.pl_bud_project = view.project;
Q.pl_bud_reason = view.reason;
Q.pl_bud_necessary = view.necessary ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_bud_forecast = view.forecast;
Q.pl_bud_vote = view.vote;
for (var option of ['protect', 'wealth', 'loan']) {
    Q['pl_bud_' + option + '_why'] = PolishProjects.budgetOptionStatus(Q, option).reason;
}
!}

= The cabinet's package

Because [+ pl_bud_reason +], the cabinet proposes: [+ pl_bud_package +][? if pl_bud_project : , with [+ pl_bud_project +] ?]. The Sejm votes at the settlement of [+ pl_bud_vote +]. Budget: [+ pl_bud_forecast +].

[? if pl_bud_necessary : The premier treats this package as necessary: if it is refused, he presents one revision, and resigns if that fails too. ?]

A condition of PPS is judged by the cabinet's partners. If they refuse it, PPS votes against the package; if PPS votes were needed, the package falls.

- @support
- @protect
- @wealth
- @loan
- @refuse
- @later

@support
title: Support the package as proposed
subtitle: PPS shares the responsibility for the policy it supports.
on-arrival: {!
var answer = PolishProjects.answerBudget(Q, 'support');
Q.pl_bud_result = 'PPS will vote for the package.';
!}
go-to: result

@protect
title: Protect workers' spending
subtitle: The package without the cut of benefits; the budget loses that saving.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.budgetOptionStatus(Q, 'protect').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_bud_protect_why +]
on-arrival: {!
var answer = PolishProjects.answerBudget(Q, 'protect');
Q.pl_bud_result = (answer.accepted ? 'The partners accept: the cut of benefits leaves the package, and PPS will vote for it.' :
    'The partners refuse; PPS will vote against the package.') + ' ' + PolishGovernment.describeAnswers({evaluations: answer.evaluations});
!}
go-to: result

@wealth
title: Shift the burden to wealth
subtitle: A progressive tax or the extraordinary wealth tax instead of burdens on broad groups; business pressure grows (+4 or +8).
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.budgetOptionStatus(Q, 'wealth').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_bud_wealth_why +]
on-arrival: {!
var answer = PolishProjects.answerBudget(Q, 'wealth');
Q.pl_bud_result = (answer.accepted ? 'The partners accept the tax on wealth instead; PPS will vote for the package.' :
    'The partners refuse; PPS will vote against the package.') + ' ' + PolishGovernment.describeAnswers({evaluations: answer.evaluations});
!}
go-to: result

@loan
title: Propose a loan instead of cuts
subtitle: A domestic loan: brings the budget 3 units a month for six months, then costs it 1 unit a month for twelve months. Needs credit of at least 40.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.budgetOptionStatus(Q, 'loan').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_bud_loan_why +]
on-arrival: {!
var answer = PolishProjects.answerBudget(Q, 'loan');
Q.pl_bud_result = (answer.accepted ? 'The partners accept the loan instead of the cuts; PPS will vote for the package.' :
    'The partners refuse; PPS will vote against the package.') + ' ' + PolishGovernment.describeAnswers({evaluations: answer.evaluations});
!}
go-to: result

@refuse
title: Refuse
subtitle: PPS does not support the package.
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.answerBudget(Q, 'refuse');
Q.pl_bud_result = 'PPS will vote against the package.';
!}
go-to: result

@later
title: Not now
subtitle: Without an answer PPS votes as its role binds it.
go-to: main

@result
new-page: true

= The cabinet's package

[+ pl_bud_result +]

- @root: Continue.
